These assets are loaded from the host or fetched into ignored local preview caches;
their original licenses remain applicable. The static framing editor also serves pinned
framework, MapLibre and font assets with the full original licenses in framing/licenses/.
The included TRMNL, Inter and Nico fonts use SIL Open Font License 1.1.
No tile archive is redistributed.

AISStream: aggregate evaluation counts are included in docs/coverage; no vessel-record
dataset is bundled. The limited latest-value display proxy follows AISStream’s published
server-side proxy guidance (https://aisstream.io/, checked 6 November 2026). No general
open-data, archival redistribution or resale licence is claimed. Scope and unresolved
terms: deploy/aisstream-rights.json and docs/data-source-evaluation.md.
Synthetic demo data is not observed traffic.

Optional vessel reference facts and exact UN/LOCODE resolutions: Wikidata,
CC0 structured data: https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Wikidata:Licensing
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
Each enriched card links to its source entity and preserves its fetch date.
No Wikimedia photographs are bundled or assumed to have a blanket license.
Digitraffic Portnet reported previous-port records retain source/date and the
same Fintraffic CC BY 4.0 attribution above; unrelated personal/agent/customs
fields are neither stored nor distributed. Free enrichment is optional.

Country-aware optional reference facts also use CC0 Wikidata structured data,
including country-qualified ports, maritime radio-assignment areas, registry
references and identified shipyard countries. Inferences are labeled and retain
provenance. Reported nationality codes from relevant Finnish Portnet calls retain
Fintraffic CC BY 4.0 attribution. AIS ETA year inference is a separate derived
heuristic; original yearless reported values and timestamps are preserved.

Curated port blurbs are original factual summaries; per-fact reference URLs are
retained in port_of_call/port_facts.py and API metadata. Exact LVMRX resolution
(Mērsrags, Latvia) follows UNECE UN/LOCODE, checked against its published CSV mirror.

Bundled coded-location names: Wikidata structured data, CC0, retrieved on
11 November 2026 from the public QLever Wikidata mirror and official Wikidata
query service. Per-entry entity IDs, query text, source hashes and exclusions
are retained in port_of_call/_locode_data.py and docs/port-reference-snapshot.json.
https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Wikidata:Licensing
https://qlever.dev/wikidata
No wholesale UNECE directory is included. These names do not supply vessel positions.
